Hi Alex,

I know I ask too many questions. Thank you for your patience response, Alex. I'm stuck again. I used the getMembers function and got the output but I don't know how to interpret it. Can you help with this problem too?

20 Mayıs 2024 Pazartesi tarihinde saat 06:23:59 UTC-4 itibarıyla Alexander Blume şunları yazdı:

> Hi Tuba,
>
> Your annotated object "diffAnn.hypo/hyper"  includes a binary membership matrix telling you if a CpG was annotated as promoter, exon or intron. You can access this matrix using the getMembers function and use it to subset your original myDiff.hypo/hyper objects.
>
> Alternatively, you can also follow the approach outlined at https://chitka-kalyan.blogspot.com/2014/10/extending-methylkit-extract-promoters.html and extend this for exon and intron respectively.
>
> Best,
> Alex
>
>
>
> Tuba schrieb am Sonntag, 19. Mai 2024 um 12:38:11 UTC+2:
> > Hi Alex,
> >
> > Thank you for your answer, I have one more question.
> > How can I see the hyper/hypo methylation in promoter/exon/intron separately?
> >
> > Thank you for your help,
> > Tuba
> > 13 Mayıs 2024 Pazartesi tarihinde saat 04:25:59 UTC-4 itibarıyla Alexander Blume şunları yazdı:
> > > Hi Tuba,
> > >
> > > if you used the myDiff25p.hypo object to generate the diffAnn.hypo object, then yes, in theory, they should have the same number of rows. However, only 25634 of your 25707 sites could be assigned to a TSS. A simple reason for not finding a TSS-CpG association could be that there is no annotated gene on the given contig for your genome.
> > > The direct mapping between the two files is given by the 'target.row' column of tss.assoc.hypo, which contains the original row number of myDiff25p.hypo. Using this column, you should be able to figure out which rows are are missing and which contigs failed.
> > >
> > > I hope this helps.
> > >
> > > Best,
> > > Alex
> > >
> > > Am So., 12. Mai 2024 um 15:28 Uhr schrieb Tuba <tuuba....@gmail.com>:
> > > > Hi Alex,
> > > >
> > > >
> > > > I tried “myDiff25p.hypo=getMethylDiff(myDiff,difference=25,qvalue=0.01,type="hypo")” command and “tss.assoc.hypo <- getAssociationWithTSS (diffAnn.hypo)” command.  Row numbers are not equal from the files obtain with command outputs. Don't the line numbers of the two output files correspond exactly? Are there losses? I am confused. Can you help with this?
> > > >
> > > > Thank you in advance for your help,
> > > >
> > > > Tuba
> > > > 10 Nisan 2024 Çarşamba tarihinde saat 04:02:29 UTC-4 itibarıyla Alexander Blume şunları yazdı:
> > > > > Hi Tuba,
> > > > >
> > > > > The myDiff25p object contains this information.
> > > > > If you want the ranges, you could convert it to a GRanges object using GRanges(). You can also export the result to a bedgraph file via bedgraph() function.
> > > > >
> > > > > Best,
